<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đinh Liễn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–979</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Dinh Lien</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đinh Liễn was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Đinh Tiên Hoàng</a>, the first emperor of the Đinh dynasty of Đại Cồ Việt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. He served his father as a commander and envoy, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> court gave him the title of prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozhi">Giao Chỉ</a> in the 970s. In 979 he and his father were murdered by the official Đỗ Thích, a killing that opened the way for the seizure of power by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Lê Hoàn</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dinh-lien.jpg" alt="Đinh Liễn" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kien1980v at Vietnamese Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinhlien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
